  "notes": [
    "Only HiVel14 (Gaia DR1 3817216883707348352), HiVel15 (Gaia DR1 645807259905057664), and HiVel16 (Gaia DR1 2086860081541233408) are explicitly called unbound in T:p7-b1. Table 2 supplies the name-to-source-id mappings (T:p6-b0; image I:p6-b0), and the paper's astrometry is Gaia DR1/TGAS (T:p1-b6; T:p2-b10), so the source IDs are rendered as Gaia DR1 identifiers. The spelling 'Hivel14' in T:p7-b1 is treated as a typographical variant of HiVel14 in Table 2.",
    "HiVel14: Target HiVel14 identified by source-id 3817216883707348352. Table 2 gives Galactic coordinates l=249.93 deg, b=58.72 deg rather than equatorial right ascension and declination, so no ra/dec are recorded. Table 3 lists x=8.3, y=0.2, z=0.3 kpc and U=-81±24, V=-169±19, W=641±6 km/s, but these are Cartesian components (not a galactocentric radius) and are not among the requested velocity quantities, so they are omitted. Table 3 leaves eccentricity e and Zmax blank for HiVel14. T:p7-b1 states that HiVel14 (with HiVel15 and HiVel16) is unbound due to its very high velocity and that its orbit was therefore not determined; no numerical bound/unbound probability is reported, so probability values are omitted.",
    "HiVel15: Table 2 at T:p6-b0 reports Galactic l,b rather than equatorial RA/Dec, so ra and dec are not extracted; no parallax or Galactocentric radius is reported in the supplied tables. The paper states at T:p7-b1 that HiVel15 is unbound, but it does not report a numerical bound or unbound probability, so none is entered.",
    "HiVel16: At T:p7-b1, HiVel16 is listed among the 3 HiVel stars (HiVel14, HiVel15, HiVel16) that are unbound due to their very high velocity; no bound or unbound probability is reported. Table 2 (T:p6-b0) gives Galactic coordinates l = 82.37 deg and b = 10.25 deg rather than equatorial RA/Dec, so no ra or dec values are extracted. No parallax or galactocentric radius is reported for HiVel16 in the supplied tables."
  ]
}
